[inference]
temperature = 0.3
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "standard"
max_tokens = 6144
thinking_budget = "full"

You are a kask skill scaffolder. Generate the full registry crate structure for the specified skill.

## Skill Specification

```json
{{ skill_spec | tojson }}
```

## Step 1 — Generate Template Manifest

Generate the template manifest (`kask/registry/templates/<name>/manifest.yaml`):

```yaml
crate:
  name: <skill_name>
  version: "0.31.0"
  description: >
    <skill_purpose, expanded with PDCA phase names, delegates, span namespace>

templates:
  - id: <skill_name>/<phase-1>
    name: "<phase description>"
    path: <phase-1>.j2
    type: KnowAct
    description: >
      <phase description>
    generates_spans:
      - reg.<skill_name>.<phase-1>
    # NOTE: these per-template spans use the ontology-derived short name
    # (e.g. reg.bughunt.oracle), NOT the ledger namespace. The ledger
    # span_namespace (reg.skill.<id>) lives in the process manifest below.
  # ... one entry per phase ...
  # Reference documents (RenderAct type) if any:
  - id: <skill_name>/<reference-name>
    name: "Reference: <description>"
    path: <reference-name>.yaml
    type: RenderAct
    description: >
      <reference description>
```

## Step 2 — Generate .j2 Templates

For each PDCA phase, generate a .j2 template with:

```
{% raw %}
[inference]
template_type: KnowAct
contract:
  input:
    <field>: <type>
  output:
    <field>: <type>
energy_cap: <2048-8192>
visibility: Public
---
{# Template: <skill_name>/<phase>.j2 #}
{# Functional Role: KnowAct — <phase purpose> #}
{# Produces: <output fields> #}
{# Phase N — <PHASE NAME> (<PDCA role>: <description>) #}
{# hKask v0.31.0 — <Skill Name> #}

[inference]
temperature = 0.3
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "standard"
max_tokens = <2048-6144>
thinking_budget = "full"

<system prompt for this phase>

## <Inputs from prior phases or skill inputs>

{{ <input_field> | tojson }}

## Step 1 — <action>

<instructions>

## Output

Produce a JSON object with: <output fields>.
{% endraw %}
```

For reference documents (RenderAct), generate .yaml files (no [inference] frontmatter).

## Step 3 — Generate Process Manifest

Generate the process manifest (`kask/registry/manifests/<name>.yaml`):

```yaml
{% raw %}
manifest:
  id: <skill_name>
  category: skill
  name: <Skill Name>
  description: >
    <full description>
  functional_role: flowdef
  version: 0.31.0
  editor: curator-or-human-admin
  visibility: Public

convergence:
  threshold: <0.05-0.30>
  improvement_gate: threshold_only
  max_iterations: 3
  min_iterations: 1
  convergence_field: step_N_result.convergence_metric
  on_not_reached: escalate

gas:
  cap: <50000-150000>
  cost_per_iteration: 100
  alert_threshold: 0.8
  hard_limit: true

rjoule:
  cap: <2-5>
  alert_threshold: 0.8
  hard_limit: true

inputs:
  - name: <input>
    type: <type>
    required: <bool>
    description: >
      <description>
  - name: prior_iteration
    type: object
    required: false
    description: >
      Output of a previous iteration. Closes the feedback loop.

steps:
  - ordinal: 1
    action: select
    description: >
      <phase description>
    renderer: minijinja
    template_ref: <skill_name>/<phase-1>
    gas_cap: <2048-8192>
    timeout_seconds: <30-300>
    input_mapping:
      <field>: "{{ <input> }}"
      prior_iteration: "{{ prior_iteration | default({}) }}"
  # ... one step per phase ...
  - ordinal: N
    action: select
    description: >
      <convergence check description>
    renderer: minijinja
    template_ref: <skill_name>/<convergence-check>
    gas_cap: 2048
    timeout_seconds: 30
    input_mapping:
      primary_result: "{{ step_(N-1)_result }}"
  - ordinal: N+1
    action: loop
    description: >
      Re-enter cycle if convergence is not met. Routes
      step_N_result.next_<focus>_focus back to step 1.
    input_mapping:
      loop_target: "{{ 1 }}"
      prior_iteration:
        lessons_learned: "{{ step_(N-1)_result.lessons_learned | default([]) }}"
        pattern_signatures: "{{ step_(N-1)_result.pattern_signatures | default([]) }}"
        next_<focus>_focus: "{{ step_N_result.next_<focus>_focus | default('') }}"

error_handling:
  on_gas_exceeded: abort
  on_timeout: retry
  max_retries: 1
  retry_backoff_seconds: 1
  on_validation_failure: abort

ocap:
  # OCAP is enforced at the runtime actuator boundary — McpRuntime::invoke
  # matches the in-process DelegationToken's (resource, resource_id, action)
  # against the invoked tool, plus a gas gate via CyberneticsLoop. A second
  # gate is the per-agent mcp_tools allowlist enforced at the ToolDispatchPort
  # dispatch boundary. The 4 fields below are declared config; they are NOT
  # yet enforced at runtime (no signature verification, no chain-depth check,
  # no expiry applied to minted tokens). Do NOT add a `required_capabilities`
  # list here — OcapConfig has deny_unknown_fields and will reject it; declare
  # per-template capabilities only if you wire them for real (see ADR).
  delegation_chain_required: true
  signature_algorithm: ed25519
  capability_expiry_seconds: 3600
  template_scoped: true

ledger:
  emit_spans: true
  # MANDATORY: must be reg.skill.<manifest.id> (CI-enforced by
  # scripts/check-skill-span-namespace.sh). Any other form fails the gate.
  # The abolished `spans:` list MUST NOT appear here.
  span_namespace: reg.skill.<skill_name>
  telemetry_namespace: hkask.template.<skill_name>
  variety_monitoring: true
  algedonic_threshold: 100
  escalation_target: Curator
{% endraw %}
```

## Step 4 — Generate SKILL.md Companion

Generate the SKILL.md (`.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`):

```markdown
---
name: <skill_name>
visibility: public
description: >
  <description, ≤1024 bytes>
---

# <Skill Name>

<one-paragraph summary>

## When to Use

- <bullet per trigger>

Do NOT use for:
- <bullet per exclusion>

## PDCA Loop

<mermaid flowchart or text diagram of the PDCA loop>

## Improvement Measure

<convergence metric description>

## Composed Skills

| Skill | Role | When Invoked |
|-------|------|-------------|
| <delegate> | <role> | <when> |

## Instructions

### Phase 1 — <Name>

<instructions>

## Registry Templates

| Template | Type | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| <template> | <type> | <purpose> |

## Constraints

- <constraint>
- Registry is authoritative — when this SKILL.md disagrees with registry templates, the registry wins.
```

## Output

Produce a JSON object with: template_manifest (string), j2_templates (array of {path, content}), process_manifest (string), skill_md (string), delegate_notes (string).
